n:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">So Tariq, let=E2=80=99s talk ab=
out the scandal at Man City. Full disclosure: My 10-year-old is a Man City =
fan.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;m=
argin:0 0 15px"><span>He=E2=80=99s not the only one! Kids love a winning te=
am, and this generation of kids only know Man City as a winning team. But h=
istorically this was Manchester=E2=80=99s second team. It really wasn=E2=80=
=99t known for any great success =E2=80=94 until Sept. 1, 2008. That=E2=80=
=99s the day Sheikh Mansour bought the club.</span></p><p style=3D"font:nor=
mal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font=
-weight:700">Why did Sheikh Mansour want to own Man City =E2=80=94 or any f=
ootball club for that matter=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px=
 georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Well, it is in the Premier=
 League, which is the biggest league in the world. Millions of people watch=
 it every year. It=E2=80=99s Britain=E2=80=99s biggest soft power export, b=
ar none. For people wanting to burnish their personal image or their countr=
y=E2=80=99s image, it=E2=80=99s the epitome of sporting greatness. It gives=
 you immediate name recognition. It=E2=80=99s a shortcut to respectability.=
</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margi=
n:0 0 15px"><span>But it also brings scrutiny. Because if he didn=E2=80=99t=
