=80=99t watch the Premier League, what happened=3F</span></p><p style=3D"fo=
nt:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>It=E2=
=80=99s massive. It=E2=80=99s the biggest financial cheating scandal in the=
 history of football. To put it simply, they cooked the books in order to s=
pend money they weren=E2=80=99t allowed to spend on an array of world-class=
 talent.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#3=
33;margin:0 0 15px"><span>You can only spend what you earn. There are three=
 buckets of income for football teams: TV rights, stadium tickets and spons=
orship. The first two, you can=E2=80=99t really manipulate. The third one i=
s, according to a panel of arbitrators, the one that they really went to to=
wn on.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333=
;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">How so=3F</span></p><p st=
yle=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><spa=
n>They signed a bunch of sham contracts with sponsors =E2=80=94 U.A.E.-owne=
d companies, like Etihad Airways. But those companies paid for a tiny fract=
ion of that sponsorship. The rest of it came from Sheikh Mansour=E2=80=99s =
company, which was padding those numbers to an enormous degree. Of the roug=
hly 950 million pounds of supposed sponsorship money Man City was claiming,=
 only 120 million or so actually came from sponsors.</span></p><p style=3D"=
font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=
=3D"font-weight:700">And all that money allowed it to buy players it would =
otherwise not have been able to afford=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal=
 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Exactly. It allo=
wed City to buy one of the best managers, Pep Guardiola, and some of the be=
st players =E2=80=94 Kevin De Bruyne, David Silva, Sergio Aguero =E2=80=94 =
and pay them some of the biggest wages in the business. They=E2=80=99ve won=
 eight Premier League titles under Sheikh Mansour=E2=80=99s ownership.</spa=
n></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0=
 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">So who was hurt by this=3F</span></p=
><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px=
"><span>Where to start=3F Man City took the best players from so many rival=
 teams over the years. From its traditional rival, Manchester United, from =
Arsenal, but also from mid-ranking teams like Aston Villa, who for three su=
